## **Strategic Value**

The BFSI AI Governance Handbook is positioned as the primary consulting and executive education asset emerging from the P3 research programme. By translating Regulatory Parallelism, Governance Debt, and the coordination typology into operational tools, it converts an academic contribution into a practitioner-facing governance framework. The handbook creates a differentiated advisory position focused on multi-regulator governance complexity rather than conventional AI risk management alone. As a consulting anchor, it supports workshops, governance diagnostics, executive briefings, advisory retainers, and long-term thought-leadership positioning within the Indian BFSI sector.

